<title>UK: HSBC shares jump as results beat forecast. [CORRECTED 11:26 GMT]</title>
<headline>HSBC shares jump as results beat forecast. [CORRECTED 11:26 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HSBC Holdings Plc, the world's biggest financial services group by most measures, soared on Monday after the bank announced profits and dividends ahead of expectations.</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit in sterling terms rose 13 percent to 2.623 billion (corrects from &quot;million&quot;) pounds while the first half dividend was up 33 percent to 20 pence per share.</p>
</text>
